note <the compiler fuzzed: mutated programs fed to the live compiler, which must always answer and never throw>

# The checks of deck/test/code/demo-compiler-fuzz.ts (decision 004, term-cli-in-term-0114), its budget and seed: 3,000
# mutated inputs from the default corpus at seed 7, four mutations each. The fuzzer ran the full budget; it reached
# three or more distinct diagnostic codes (real coverage); and every input was classified: a crash is a finding the
# demo listed rather than failed on, so the check is that each crash carries the input and the error that make it one.
# The demo's fourth outcome, a HANG caught by a watchdog over a child process, has no form here: the campaign runs in
# the test's own process, so a compiler that never answered would stall the test, which is itself the finding. The
# compiler is docked by compiler-fuzzing.tree: `term test` builds the module inside the project, whose tsconfig maps
# the dock to its source (decision 009).

load ../code/compiler-fuzzing
  find fuzz-compiler
  find fuzz-corpus
  find fuzz-ask
  find fuzz-report

load @term/base/list
  find list

task campaign
  like fuzz-report

  back fuzz-compiler(make(fuzz-ask, bind(corpus, fuzz-corpus()), bind(runs, 3000), bind(seed, 7), bind(mutations-per-run, 4), bind(probe-file, <>), bind(has-budget, false), bind(perf-budget-ms, 0)))

test <the fuzzer runs its full budget, reaches three or more diagnostics, and classifies every input>
  host report, campaign()
  want hold, is-equal report/runs, 3000
  want hold, is-minimum report/codes-seen/length, 3
  save classified, true
  walk report/crashes
    take each
    fork test, or(is-equal(each/input, <>), is-equal(each/error, <>))
      hold
        save classified, false
  want hold, classified
